{{- /* sitemap.xml, for a site that has more than one language.

       Hugo builds this file as a <sitemapindex>: a list pointing at the
       per-language sitemaps, each of which is the real <urlset>. That is what
       the standard describes, it is what Google follows, and it is what this
       template still emits by default.

       It is also a shape a crawler has to know to follow, and a good number of
       them do not. They fetch /sitemap.xml, take every <loc> out of it and read
       each one as a page — so the pages they end up auditing are the two
       sub-sitemaps, which are XML: no <title>, no JSON-LD, no prose, no lists.
       The site's actual content is never reached. aeo.js v0.0.16 does exactly
       this — its crawlPages() feeds every <loc> straight into the page audit —
       and measured against a bilingual site it cost 12 of 100 points for
       content the build already publishes: the one post it never opened
       carries a BlogPosting node and a <ul>.

       `[params.aeo] flatSitemap = true` publishes one <urlset> at the root
       instead, listing every page of every language with its hreflang
       alternates. Nothing is given up by doing so: the per-language sitemaps
       are still built and still served at their own URLs, and the 50,000-URL
       ceiling that makes an index necessary is not one a typical site
       approaches. It is off by default for the reason robots.txt gives for
       allowTraining — a module upgrade should not quietly change what a site
       publishes, and this file is a published contract with every crawler that
       already knows the site.

       Both branches below are Hugo's own embedded templates, kept faithful to
       v0.163: sitemap.xml for the flat one and sitemapindex.xml for the other.
       Overriding this template *replaces* the built-in, so the default branch
       has to reproduce it rather than fall through to it — which is the one
       maintenance cost here, and why the branch is written to be diffed against
       the upstream file rather than tidied.

       Context: []*hugolib.Site, one per language, in config order. A
       single-language site never renders this template at all — Hugo writes its
       sitemap.xml straight from sitemap.xml — so `flatSitemap` is inert there
       and the README says so.

       One more thing about 0.158, because it is the version theme.toml declares
       and the trap is shaped like a fix: its embedded sitemap.xml ranges over
       `.Translations` and emits a separate self-link *outside* the range, where
       0.163 ranges over `.AllTranslations`, which already includes the self.
       The two produce the same set of alternates in a different order, and
       order carries no meaning to sitemaps.org. The 0.163 form is the same
       statement made once, so it is the one copied — "correcting" it back to
       .Translations drops every self-referential hreflang, which is a real
       regression and one a grep for a single hreflang value will not see.

       Both branches drop the pages [params.aeo] disallow excludes, for the reason
       aeo-gate.html gives: a sitemap is an invitation to fetch a URL, so listing
       one that robots.txt blocks is the two files disagreeing in the direction
       that costs something — Search Console reports it as an error, and the
       exclusion was the point of the key. The index branch names sub-sitemaps
       rather than pages, so the filtering there happens in sitemap.xml, which
       this module also ships for exactly that reason.

       `site` here is sites[0] — the first language by weight, *not*
       defaultContentLanguage — which is a distinction this file does not want
       to depend on. It reads `(index . 0)` instead, so the code says what it
       means, and then checks every other language for a flatSitemap that
       disagrees. This is one file for the whole site: it can only be flat or
       not, and a per-language override is a statement that cannot be honoured.
       The README says to write the param at the root; this is what happens when
       someone follows the `[languages.<lang>.params…]` pattern the README
       teaches everywhere else instead. Silence there would be exactly the
       failure aeo-params-bool.html exists to prevent. */ -}}
{{- $primary := index . 0 -}}
{{- $aeo := partial "aeo-params-table.html" (dict "value" $primary.Params.aeo "path" "[params.aeo]") -}}
{{- $flat := partial "aeo-params-bool.html" (dict "value" $aeo.flatSitemap "path" "[params.aeo] flatSitemap" "default" false) -}}
{{- /* A root [params.aeo] is merged into every language, so a site that wrote
       the param once agrees with itself here and says nothing. Only a genuine
       per-language override reaches the warning. */ -}}
{{- range . -}}
  {{- $own := (partial "aeo-params-table.html" (dict "value" .Params.aeo "path" "[params.aeo]")).flatSitemap -}}
  {{- if and (ne $own nil) (ne $own $flat) -}}
    {{- warnf "aeo-hugo: [languages.%s.params.aeo] flatSitemap = %v is ignored — /sitemap.xml is one file for the whole site, and %s wins as the first language by weight. Set it in [params.aeo] at the root instead." .Language.Lang $own $primary.Language.Lang -}}
  {{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{ printf "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>" | safeHTML }}
{{- $disallow := partial "aeo-params-list.html" (dict "value" $aeo.disallow "path" "[params.aeo] disallow" "maps" false) -}}
{{- if $flat }}
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9"
  xmlns:xhtml="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
  {{- range . }}
  {{- /* Each language's pages against that language's own root: this template is
         rendered once for every site at once, so the `site` global aeo-allowed
         reads by default is whichever language came first, and a Portuguese page
         measured against the English root is excluded by nothing. */ -}}
  {{- range partial "aeo-allowed.html" (dict "pages" (where .Pages "Sitemap.Disable" "ne" true) "disallow" $disallow "root" .Home.RelPermalink) }}
    {{- if .Permalink }}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ .Permalink }}</loc>{{ if not .Lastmod.IsZero }}
    <lastmod>{{ safeHTML ( .Lastmod.Format "2006-01-02T15:04:05-07:00" ) }}</lastmod>{{ end }}{{ with .Sitemap.ChangeFreq }}
    <changefreq>{{ . }}</changefreq>{{ end }}{{ if ge .Sitemap.Priority 0.0 }}
    <priority>{{ .Sitemap.Priority }}</priority>{{ end }}{{ if .IsTranslated }}{{ range .AllTranslations }}
    <xhtml:link
                rel="alternate"
                hreflang="{{ .Language.Locale }}"
                href="{{ .Permalink }}"
                />{{ end }}{{ end }}
  </url>
    {{- end }}
  {{- end }}
  {{- end }}
</urlset>
{{- else }}
<sitemapindex xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  {{- range . }}
  <sitemap>
    <loc>{{ .SitemapAbsURL }}</loc>{{ if not .Lastmod.IsZero }}
    <lastmod>{{ .Lastmod.Format "2006-01-02T15:04:05-07:00" | safeHTML }}</lastmod>{{ end }}
  </sitemap>
  {{- end }}
</sitemapindex>
{{- end }}
